WEBVTT

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.770
So, what is all this?

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.860
Dumplings, obviously.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.570
You bought this many?!

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.880
Don't be silly. You're buying them.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.070
Huh? Why me?

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:48.740
As an apology for your failure the other day, obviously.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:51.230
Having us infiltrate a fortress for no reason.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.630
Leaving behind a hero's relic we found without even using it.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.520
You're buying dumplings for me every day from now on, got it?

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.540
You left it right along with me! What were we supposed to do?

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:06.910
Do you think using a hero's relic that's been resting for centuries is easy?

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.820
Besides, how does that relate to buying dumplings—

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.360
Yes, ma'am. I'll buy them. It would be my pleasure.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.850
Very good.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:17.010
Thank you, come again.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:21.720
Why is this happening to me? Damn it! This is all Sion's fault!

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.280
He keeps pushing one pain in the ass after another on me!

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.670
I'll bet he's having a nice meal in the castle right about now, or a lazy afternoon nap.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:45.390
Your Majesty, how do you intend to take responsibility for this matter?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:49.240
Watch your tone when addressing His Majesty!

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.060
You even guaranteed that the populace would keep their lifestyle.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.680
That sort of attitude ferments—

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.570
Be silent!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.680
The boss makes his appearance.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.390
I beg your pardon, Your Majesty, but he also worries about the kingdom.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.620
I undertand. Don't worry about it.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:17.570
As such, how do you plan to deal with this revolt?

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.220
I have high hopes for a prompt response.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.420
A prompt response?

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.420
It's only been two days since we first received notice.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:29.980
We don't even know the location of the rebel army's stronghold or its ringleader.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.430
He's an irritating bastard.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.680
Countermeasures have already been deployed.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.130
We've done research on the ringleader of the revolt.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:41.610
The only daughter of the old king of Estabul, Lady Noa Ehn.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:45.600
Colonel Miran Froaude will fill you in on the information he gathered.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.410
According to our intelligence, the Estabul side has roughly fifty thousand soldiers.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.520
Fifty thousand!

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.410
That goes beyond any revolt. It's a war!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:01.520
It is likely that territories adjacent to Estabul will be caught in the fighting.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.330
For the time being, we'd like to have you evacuated to this castle.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.220
We shall be certain to protect all of your territories.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.110
You say to leave our territory?!

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:13.100
Are you lot saying you would trample our lands?

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.570
I will never permit it!

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:18.730
Do you have something you would prefer we did not see?

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.750
C-Certainly not...

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.910
You are free to remain there if you prefer, of course.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:28.230
Estabul's forces are only fifty thousand at most. Nothing to fear, surely.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.720
Your Majesty, I will be taking the army.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.590
We will guard each territory, and supress the revolt.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:41.000
No, I shall place Rear Admiral Claugh Klom in charge of handling this matter.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:44.550
Consider it done.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.270
Froaude, take care of information gathering and dissemination.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.860
Offer Claugh your counsel.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.890
Have this guy supporting me?!

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.330
That's an order, Claugh.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.410
Froaude, am I understood?

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:55.390
Sir.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.560
Your Majesty.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:02.270
What is this about?

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:05.080
You set up this revolt, didn't you?

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.000
Spark a revolt among interested parties,

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.120
then make a clean sweep of all the anti-Roland forces at once.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.520
Using this war as an excuse to send soldiers to every territory

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.160
and pry into the misdeeds of the nobles of the anti-king faction.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.170
If that were the case, what would you do?

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.730
I'd do nothing.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.650
You focus on your own job. Nothing more.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:36.590
My father is still in Roland?

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:38.680
Are you concerned for your father?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.180
Your father, our king,

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:47.790
sold out his kingdom readily, in exchange for status and safety given to him by Roland.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.860
I know.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:54.750
But I think the people would be happier if Father led the revolt.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:59.450
We nobles, and the people, all adore you greatly.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:02.290
Our new lord, Lady Noa Ehn.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.300
Leave it at that.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.390
Are you afraid?

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:11.440
I am afraid. What will happen if we don't win this battle?

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:14.890
Roland's treated the people of Estabul well.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.740
Is fighting really necessary?

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:21.030
Of course it is. To save the historic Estabul from Roland—

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.780
I don't care what happens to the kingdom! The people come first!

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.570
Will this really make the people happy?

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.940
Isn't it just excessive bloodshed?

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.550
I'll be satisfied if the people could live happily.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:36.990
Aren't you the one who taught me that, Salawell?

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:39.980
Right now, our forces are still strong.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.810
So, Roland won't get too brazen.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.860
But there's no guarantee of that in the future.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.740
I've heard terrible rumors about the Roland nobility, too.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.730
If you truly want to consider the people, now is the time.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:56.140
If you speak thus, it must be so.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:00.470
For you, I would not shrink even from death.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.980
I want to make a kingdom

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.140
where everyone can live with a smile.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:08.730
Where everyone can be happy!

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:10.710
Can I do it, Salawell?

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:12.150
Of course you can!

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:30.150
We shall henceforth do battle with Roland!

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:33.880
We shall take back Estabul's independence ourselves!

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.680
Yeah!

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:39.350
I bear a message from Rear Admiral Klom!

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.170
The battle has commenced!

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.240
Shuss, what are the enemy's numbers?

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.330
Roughly eight to nine thousand.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.730
It's exactly as Froaude's information said.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:06.910
I don't like it.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:07.630
Sir?

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:11.860
Nothing. We'll take this place with minimal casualties.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:12.710
Let's go!

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.180
All forces, advance!

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.500
The dogs of Roland!

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.970
What rock did they crawl out from under?!

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:23.990
We can't use any big spells in a close quarters battle like this!

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:26.110
Out of the way!

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:27.920
Where are they? Where's the commander?!

00:08:38.590 --> 00:08:42.060
Is it you? Are you this army's commander?!

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:43.130
You're—

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:51.690
I just made mincemeat of your Estabul commander.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.140
If you resist any further, I'll kill you all.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:58.410
That bloodstained red ring... It's Crimson-Fingered Claugh!

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:01.090
That's Crimson-Fingered Claugh, of Roland!

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:04.850
Damn it. All this pointless killing each other...

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.720
Defeated again?

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:20.140
It's like they're reading our army's every move!

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:23.360
I told you! I told you it was reckless!

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:24.550
You pick a fine moment to say it!

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:25.840
Crimson-Fingered Claugh?

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:29.330
You said Roland's commander was Claugh Klom, did you not?

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.090
Ma'am.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:35.480
From what I have heard, he has gone to extreme lengths

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:37.650
to force our men to surrender without killing them, has he not?

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:38.340
Ma'am.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.950
If that is how Roland battles...

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:43.460
If that is the will of Sion Astal, the Hero King,

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.220
then this fight is...

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:49.000
Don't be ridiculous. That's the enemy's goal, no doubt.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.800
He's right! Once they take Estabul,

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:55.330
they'll take out their anger and hatred, and lengthen the fighting.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.680
We still have a way. You must not falter, Princess.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:03.590
Rear Admiral Klom's army has surrounded the rebel army's main stronghold.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:33.110
What is the meaning of this?!

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:36.570
Withdraw Roland's army and reIease aII prisoners of war.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:40.240
lf they do not heed our demands,

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:43.400
the people of EstabuI will be beheaded on the spot.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.470
We sent a letter with that content to the Roland army.

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:51.190
Roland's Hero King couldn't stand by and let commoners die.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.270
How could you? You're...

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:54.930
I know.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:11:00.440
But this is unfortunate. I wish to protect you... Princess.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:03.090
You would take our people hostage for my sake?!

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:05.330
This is what the people want.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:07.810
If we lose now, what would happen to them?

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:11.470
How badly would the people of a defeated nation be oppressed, and disgraced?

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:16.170
And taking our people hostage brings them no disgrace?

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:19.380
Can't this be stopped?

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:21.270
It cannot be.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:30.330
l see. l am naught but a puppet ruler propped up by others.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.950
In the end, I couldn't save anyone, could I?

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:35.260
Princess!

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:37.140
The soldiers of Roland are...!

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:41.460
Our army's soldiers are attacking the Estabul fortress!

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:42.110
What did you say?!

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:50.470
Our squadrons are all assembled...

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.460
Huh? Then what squadrons are those?

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.680
Did His Majesty send reinforcements?

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:59.810
Sion said he was putting me in charge of this! There's no way he'd do that!

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:00.330
Then...

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:01.770
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:03.150
It's him?

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.500
That's impossible!

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:09.540
Crimson-Fingered Claugh would ignore the hostages and attack?

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:14.850
What do we do? If we lose after taking people hostage, we'll be executed!

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:17.790
No, we haven't lost yet...

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:20.980
Let's kill the hostages.

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:26.140
l get it. Roland doesn't think we're serious!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.250
If we kill a hostage...

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:28.490
Cease this!

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.230
But...

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:32.270
You've all done well,

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:36.440
but this is it. Let us release the hostages.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:37.770
But, Princess...

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.150
I shall do all I can.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:41.640
With my life alone!

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.560
You must not! I cannot allow the Princess to die alone...

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:49.080
I, too... I shall accompany you, Princess!

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.050
Me, too!

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:50.690
Princess!

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:53.600
Your words alone are enough.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:54.380
Princess...

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:57.600
All of you, please live on.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:02.050
And try to give the people of Estabul at least a little bit of happiness.

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.670
For that, I would...

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:07.060
You've created a problem for me.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:11.720
All of your cares for your kingdom are quite moving.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:16.310
However, in my view, Lady Noa Ehn's life alone isn't enough

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:19.320
to atone for all of your crimes.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:24.490
Yes, is a tragedy not the most fitting adornment

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.990
for the tragedy of the kingdom of Estabul perishing?

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.150
Who are you?

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:33.190
I am Miran Froaude, Colonel of the Imperial Roland Army.

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:34.450
How did you get here?

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:36.640
Did you kill every soldier outside?

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:40.710
Certainly not. This castle wouldn't fall so easily.

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:45.340
Of course, even if it did fall, Roland soldiers still couldn't come inside.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:46.480
After all...

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:51.150
...this place will now play a part in the finale of the tragedy.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.130
Let there be darkness!

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:05.460
Protect the princess!

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:06.290
Got it!

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:07.790
But we can't leave everyone...

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:17.250
Get inside!

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:25.380
Everyone's dead.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:30.680
The kingdom... The people... Everything's been lost.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.480
No, there's still something left.

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:35.430
What do we have left?

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:38.500
Your life.

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:42.880
The cornered Estabul soldiers riot.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:45.270
They begin killing hostages.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:46.520
Salawell?

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:50.820
The one commanding the riot is you, Princess.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.750
No... does that mean...?

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:56.360
And the one to kill the rioting princess and end the battle,

00:14:56.360 --> 00:15:00.340
the Estabul noble, Salawell Seile,

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:04.110
is greeted by Roland as the savior of the kingdom.

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:07.130
So making our armies meet in combat,

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.820
and suggesting we take hostages...

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:11.610
That was all your doing?

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.590
I trusted you.

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:18.930
At first, though, I planned to make you my wife and take control of this kingdom.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:24.120
All I wanted was to make a kingdom where everyone could live happily.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:25.730
And yet...

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:29.390
The world isn't moved by such pretty words.

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:31.990
Even still... Even still...!

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:35.790
How adorable you are, Princess.

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:37.650
But this is the end!

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:56.970
Please relax.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:02.780
Roland is not in need of a hero so badly that such a man could become one.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:08.830
A hero? Is this the doing of Roland's Hero King, Sion Astal?!

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:11.650
My king has no taste for such things.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:14.300
All of this is my doing alone.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:19.500
Then, the one to conspire with Salawell and lead us into revolt was...

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:21.160
Yes, it was me.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.540
He saw through it

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:26.550
and appointed Rear Admiral Klom to suppress the revolt, not me.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.010
That is the kind of man my king is.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:32.760
However, just as Salawell said,

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:35.410
it is a fact that the world isn't moved by pretty words.

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:40.360
After Lady Noa Ehn kills the hostages, she commits suicide.

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:42.360
That is how the story goes.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.100
Would King Astal forgive that?

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:47.900
Ideally, I wouldn't be found out,

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.360
but perhaps he would come to forgive it.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.380
That is a king's caliber.

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:02.040
Hey, lady. You hurt?

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.220
You're the ringleader behind this revolt?

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:08.080
You've gotten the better of me, Rear Admiral Klom.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:10.180
I wasn't expecting you to reach this place so quickly.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.590
Answer the question!

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:15.840
<i>Rear Admiral Klom? Then, this man is Crimson-Fingered Claugh?</i>

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:17.650
Depending on your answer...

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:20.180
You'll kill me, right?

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:23.070
I never thought Sion needed you anyway.

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:26.490
You don't see the burden he bears.

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:29.860
You're the one who isn't qualified to serve him.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.900
I don't need any qualifications to be at Sion's side!

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:38.100
For the sake of the path he treads, I will kill Lady Noa Ehn and the hostages.

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:41.820
If you continue to stand in my way...

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:43.870
You think you can do it?

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.700
A simple matter.

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:49.870
<i>No!</i>

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.410
<i>That power is...</i>

00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:01.700
<i>For the sake of the people of Estabul, we cannot lose this man...</i>

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:03.480
Let there...

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:04.280
<i>We mustn't!</i>

00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:06.530
Froaude!

00:18:08.010 --> 00:18:14.540
Colonel Froaude, if you must kill the hostages to completely conquer Estabul...

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:18.130
...then I'll persuade them. The people, the soldiers...

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:20.790
I'll get them to follow Roland!

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:22.750
What are you saying?

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:26.640
I think that will be far more effective

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:29.180
than killing the hostages and ruining Estabul's reputation.

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:30.850
Indeed.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:34.670
You are quite popular with the people of Estabul.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:40.040
But you might gain many detractors, calling you a traitor who sold out her kingdom.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:41.320
I don't mind.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:46.290
If you wish it, you may kill me afterwards.

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:49.530
So... Don't kill everyone, please.

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:51.400
Very well.

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.820
The battle is over.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.420
Please call off your soldiers, Rear Admiral Klom.

00:18:57.420 --> 00:18:59.280
Wait, damn you!

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.980
Hey, are you okay?

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:08.370
I believe in you, and your king.

00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:09.560
Huh?

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:17.780
Rear Admiral Klom, I can't bring myself to move.

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:19.620
Would you mind helping me stand?

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:21.430
Sure thing.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:26.490
Thank you.

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:35.440
<i>With all of you, l'm sure the people of Estabul will be...</i>

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:40.200
Again, people have died.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:44.220
Again, I have made Claugh kill people.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:49.000
I knew this war was necessary.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:52.340
That's why l didn't charge Froaude with any crimes.

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:56.890
I put Claugh in charge because I wanted to save lives, even if only a few.

00:19:56.890 --> 00:20:00.480
Or is that just my excuse?

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:02.220
Brother Sion, are you going to cry?

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:06.420
l've read about it in picture books. That's a face on the verge of tears, right?

00:20:06.420 --> 00:20:09.220
It's the first time Iris has seen one!

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:11.450
Sister Ferris never cries,

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:14.930
and brother Lucile always smiles, which is really scary!

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:18.000
Lucile is quite scary.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:20.210
Hey, are you going to cry? C'mon!

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:21.220
I won't cry.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:23.660
Did Iris come in at a bad time?

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:24.690
Maybe.

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:29.590
Okay, then next time! Next time you cry, be sure to show me!

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:33.170
Didn't you have a report from Ryner and Ferris to give me?

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:35.620
Oh, yeah. Here you go!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:43.510
The dog is Ryner, and the angel is Ferris, I take it?

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:49.080
Yup! The wild beast and the dazzling beautiful avenging angel, sister Ferris!

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:50.850
Same as always, hm?

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:52.140
What's this?

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:55.400
Uhm, they dug a hole and pulled out a dagger-looking thing.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.260
They had no idea what it was and threw it,

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:59.110
and a dragon suddenly came to life, they said!

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:03.790
A hero relic? They really existed...?

00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:06.970
Your Majesty.

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:08.550
What is it, Miller?

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:11.580
Have a look.

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:16.100
You're certain of this?

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:20.940
The information comes from him. You know who I mean, I'm sure.

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:23.150
Iris.

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:27.910
Sorry, but would you mind returning to Ryner and Ferris immediately?

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:35.740
Okay, Ryner. Take care of today's portion.

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:40.320
Dumpling, dumpling, dumpling, dumpling, dumpling!

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:44.400
Sion, you... Sion, you...!

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:49.970
Overly vulgar words are forbidden.

00:23:20.260 --> 00:23:24.640
<i>Huh? Search for the hero relic we just found again?</i>

00:23:24.640 --> 00:23:27.220
<i>What a pain! No thanks.</i>

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:30.960
<i>Why is it that everywhere we go, things always become a giant pain?</i>

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:34.370
<i>Yeesh this really sucks.</i>
